# vce_pal.vexp - the hand-derived literal rows of the vce_pal video scene (plan 04-07; D-171, D-172, ER-10, ER-11, ER-12, ER-13, F-5, F-38).
# scripts/fixture-build writes this file, comments dropped, as build/gate/fixtures/vce-pal.vexp.tsv; the runner kind video (tests/conformance/videokinds.c) reads only that file.
# One source holds the literals: no expected value lives in a case file, and none comes from a run of DuoSpool, another emulator or a hash.
# Rows are TAB separated. Four row kinds, keys closed (scripts/lib/vexp-rules.awk is the grammar):
#   scene   NAME  case=CASE_ID  role=literal|struct|golden
#   group   SCENE GID  form=ROWS|REL|STRUCT  class=MAN:<label>|GUEST:<model>|ASSUMED:<LED-id>  sym=order|asym|none  kills=F0,F5,...
#   row     SCENE GID  SELECTOR  LITERAL      (STRUCT: SELECTOR check=NAME; LITERAL key=value items separated by semicolons)
#   golden  SCENE sha256=HEX                  (one pinned stream digest of a golden scene: E0 repeatability, valid only beside a literal case of the same scene, ER-11)
# The fixture (fixtures/src/vce_pal.s) writes VCE CR $00, waits at least 5,460 master clocks (four lines; the speed is stated in vce_pal.s), writes CR $01 and writes the 512 palette entries P(i) = (91 * i + 17) & 511.
# Its groups judge headers only (the 8-dot blank window of a display line, since plan 04-09, is not judged here), so only the faults that act on a header declare a kill here: F0 (a perturbed literal), F4 (a duplicated line), F5 (a changed divider), F8 (two swapped lines), F9 (an origin moved by one clock).
# F1 F2 F3 F6 F7 act on pixels and active lines and no group of this scene reads them.
# Classes (ER-10, the weakest class of the inputs of a row wins): the struct and frame groups use the 1365-clock grid and the frame length, so they are ASSUMED (LED-VID-0004, LED-VID-0001).
# The div group is MAN H6-3 (content 00h gives division ratio 4, 01h gives 3). It is judged only on records that lie wholly at least one line (1365 clocks) after the stamp of the CR write that sets them and, between two writes, at least one line before the next one,
# so it depends neither on the grid phase nor on the tie rule; it is never judged on a record before the CR $00 write, which would rest on the power-on CR of LED-PROF-0003 (amendment A11).
# The divline group is the join of a write stamp to the grid (the tie rule of D-138), ASSUMED LED-VID-0004.
# The border group is GUEST pal_bijection: pure in-guest arithmetic over the values the guest wrote, 91 * 256 + 17 = 23313 = 45 * 512 + 273, so palette entry $100 holds 273.
# It is judged on records at least one line after the last palette data write (the stamp comes from the dev log, not from the core).
# The dirty group joins a write stamp to the grid (ASSUMED LED-VID-0004): bit 0 of line_dirty on exactly the first record after each CR write, bit 4 on exactly the first record after each palette data write.
# F0 note (A7): F0 perturbs the first number of the first row of a group, so it proves only that the comparison is live. The border group's only kill is F0, so its liveness against a changed palette store comes from the toy vid-palette-mask and not from a record fault: the toy breaks the guest readback AND the border, and since the
# review fix H-01 of the gate review the video kind judges every group past a failed guest, so the toy evidence of video_vce_pal shows the line video_group border GUEST fail (the other groups pass); the toy vid-emit-mutates shows the same line.
# The golden scene row and the golden row are a change detector beside the literal case video_vce_pal, never a verdict (ER-11): the pinned digest is the SHA-256 of the canonical stream of the vce_pal guest (D-163), measured on the first run and recomputed outside the core with a host tool (shasum -a 256 of build/gate/video/video_vce_pal.dsvr),
# E0 repeatability only. It is valid only beside the literal case of the same scene (the runner refuses video-hash-only and scripts/video-check says INV_VIDEO_HASH_ONLY otherwise). A change of the stream (a later plan that changes the records) repins it by the procedure of that plan.
# Repin of plan 04-08 (E0 change detector, ER-11): the vertical machine and the RCR counter now run, so every record carries its v_state, the ACTIVE flag on display lines, active_k and a stepping rcr_counter (the vce_pal guest leaves every vertical register at 0, so the cycle is 4 lines: 2 of VDS, 1 of VDW, 1 of VSW).
# Old digest 6c510913928bfa8703e0f5006bba728f894ccf9ce910ede9b7fcef50afd09c55, new digest c667ac7ada36e13b97178cf7a1c011e4494b6f4b3ec79359b894eafddaf35253, recomputed with shasum -a 256 over the --video-out file; the literal case video_vce_pal passed on the changed records first.
# Repin of plan 04-09 (E0 change detector, ER-11): a display line now carries its active window and payload (HDS 0, HDW 0 here, so 8 dots of index 256 and the colour of palette entry $100: rec_bytes 96 on every display line, 64 elsewhere).
# Old digest c667ac7ada36e13b97178cf7a1c011e4494b6f4b3ec79359b894eafddaf35253, new digest 03fa9142760f089c51cd33fc1a0e1cfec16547dbafcd652d40dc4cc23ddf8a85, recomputed with shasum -a 256 over the --video-out file; the literal case video_vce_pal passed on the changed records first.
# Old digest 03fa9142760f089c51cd33fc1a0e1cfec16547dbafcd652d40dc4cc23ddf8a85, new digest a33b1f0eb45e7b32c3aab68d5b08023a7c11f7c13cb77ebe4a4bb677b4802364, recomputed with shasum -a 256 over the --video-out file; the literal case video_vce_pal passed on the changed records first.
# Reason (plan 04-10): the display lines of a burst frame (CR = 0, so SB = BB = 0 at display line 0) now carry the BURST flag, the burst latch of D-157.
scene	vce_pal	case=video_vce_pal	role=literal
scene	vce_pal	case=video_vce_pal_golden	role=golden
group	vce_pal	struct	form=STRUCT	class=ASSUMED:LED-VID-0004	sym=none	kills=F4,F8,F9
row	vce_pal	struct	check=count	grid=1365
row	vce_pal	struct	check=origins	step=1365
row	vce_pal	struct	check=rec_bytes	header=64;version=1;max_w=682
row	vce_pal	struct	check=values_below_512	limit=512
group	vce_pal	frame	form=STRUCT	class=ASSUMED:LED-VID-0001	sym=none	kills=F0,F4
row	vce_pal	frame	check=frame_lines	value=262;step=1365
row	vce_pal	frame	check=records_per_frame	value=262
group	vce_pal	div	form=STRUCT	class=MAN:H6-3	sym=none	kills=F0,F5
row	vce_pal	div	check=div_table	div=4,3;crw=0,1;gap=5460
group	vce_pal	divline	form=STRUCT	class=ASSUMED:LED-VID-0004	sym=none	kills=F0,F8
row	vce_pal	divline	check=div_first	div=3;prev=4;crw=1
group	vce_pal	border	form=STRUCT	class=GUEST:pal_bijection	sym=none	kills=F0
row	vce_pal	border	check=border_after_pal	value=273
group	vce_pal	dirty	form=STRUCT	class=ASSUMED:LED-VID-0004	sym=none	kills=F0,F4
row	vce_pal	dirty	check=line_dirty	cr_bit=0;pal_bit=4
golden	vce_pal	sha256=a33b1f0eb45e7b32c3aab68d5b08023a7c11f7c13cb77ebe4a4bb677b4802364
